Description: Modern download manager for Linux with yt-dlp integration
 Leaf Downloader is a high-performance desktop download manager designed
 for Linux. It combines a custom native segmented download engine with
 yt-dlp and the elegance of GTK4 and Libadwaita.
 .
 Features include:
  - Dual download engine: IDM-style segmented HTTP downloads and full
    yt-dlp backend for 1000+ video platforms.
  - Smart Firefox browser extension with YouTube integration, universal
    video hover bar, and right-click downloads.
  - Native GNOME UI with GTK4 and Libadwaita — sidebar navigation and
    standalone download card windows with live speed graphs.
  - Intelligent clipboard monitoring — detects copied media URLs and
    offers one-click downloads.
  - Pause, resume, and cancel with crash-safe resume support via
    persistent .leafdl manifests.
  - Download queue and persistent history with JSON-based storage.
  - Configurable concurrent fragments, download directory, and API
    server settings.
 .
 yt-dlp (version 2026.3.17) is vendored inside this package and does
 not require a separate installation.
